{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The voice of YHWH makes hinds calve</b> — he mentioned the wilderness corresponding to 'in His palace' [i.e., למבול, the Flood]." "And he mentioned 'the wilderness of Kadesh' — because it is great and awesome." "And he mentioned hinds — because their giving birth is difficult, and behold the thunder causes them to calve prematurely. And the meaning: He will bring them strength quickly and they will give birth when the hind's womb opens, also because of the terror." "And the meaning of 'and strips forests bare' — He will uncover, when the trees fall." "Some say that the meaning of 'and in His palace' is the heavens, like 'YHWH in His holy palace.' And the meaning is that those who dwell in it give glory to HaShem and say: 'How great is Your glory.' And others said that the meaning concerns the priests and Levites who stand to pray. And R. Moses said: the meaning is that those who dwell in His palace — this is the Temple — and they will not fear, for HaShem will grant them honor, so that no harm will come to them because of the thunder; therefore after it: 'YHWH sat enthroned at the Flood.' And the meaning: because the waters destroyed the wicked, then the kingship of HaShem was revealed, for He executed judgment upon them; and behold HaShem will rescue His devout ones like Noah and his sons, and will kill His enemies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:56.314901394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}